WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.520
Hi, I'm Snowdrop!

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:08.263
Ring-Zero trains a one-trillion-parameter base model to reason with nothing but a checkable reward.

00:00:08.263 --> 00:00:10.313
No human-written reasoning at all.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.491
The idea: reward only a right answer and a clean format, at

00:00:15.491 --> 00:00:19.707
trillion scale, and keep it stable with four stages and one ratio fix.

00:00:21.192 --> 00:00:25.646
Stage one's loss isn't divided by length, so longer correct traces earn more credit.

00:00:25.646 --> 00:00:28.828
The model learns to think at length, and to pad.

00:00:29.248 --> 00:00:33.875
Self-distillation keeps the shortest correct traces, trims the bloat, and resets the

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:36.574
gap between the training and inference engines.

00:00:36.994 --> 00:00:40.593
Stage two divides the loss by length, so rambling earns nothing.

00:00:41.013 --> 00:00:45.534
Stage three trains three tiers, so one checkpoint reasons short or long on demand.

00:00:47.108 --> 00:00:50.656
One engine writes the rollouts, another trains on them, and they

00:00:50.656 --> 00:00:51.947
disagree by tiny amounts.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:55.899
Below the line: what the inference engine gave the token when it wrote it.

00:00:56.319 --> 00:00:58.979
Above it: what the training engine assigns now.

00:00:58.979 --> 00:01:01.639
So the ratio measures the update actually made.

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:05.714
In the ablations, a naive ratio collapsed near step eight hundred.

00:01:05.714 --> 00:01:07.043
This one kept training.

00:01:08.342 --> 00:01:09.926
Scale moves the ceiling.

00:01:09.926 --> 00:01:14.677
After stage one, the trillion-parameter model scores eighty-nine point one on AIME.

00:01:14.677 --> 00:01:17.449
The smaller flash model, seventy-one point two.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:22.133
Zero RL sharpens the reasoning already latent in pretraining.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:25.780
A bigger base, not a cleverer reward, moves the ceiling.

00:01:27.108 --> 00:01:31.205
To recap: a checkable reward, four stages that grow then trim the

00:01:31.205 --> 00:01:34.277
reasoning, and a ratio that keeps the engines honest.

00:01:34.697 --> 00:01:36.894
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:36.894 --> 00:01:37.522
I'm Snowdrop.

00:01:37.522 --> 00:01:37.836
Bye!
